<p>The time shift goes the other way. Time goes quicker, not slower. If time went slower, we'd be dealing with a Black Hole-like effect with the radiation red-shifting as it goes outwards. This acts more like a White Hole. Unfortunately, the English language still isn't equipped to handle different rates of time flow, so confusion can still happen.</p>
<p>As for the resonance frequency, physics is already a little bit screwed up inside there. I think I'll tweak that sentence a bit, though. Change it so that it's consistent with the resonance frequency, rather than being created from it.</p>

